  "result": "All five tests pass, covering both test files.\n\nChanges to `netgraph/graph.py`:\n\n- **remove_edge** removes the edge from both adjacency sets, decrements the edge counter, and returns whether an edge existed. A self-loop lives in one set, so the two discards are harmless there.\n- **degree** returns the size of the node's adjacency set. A self-loop appears once in that set, so it counts once as required.\n- **connected_components** runs a depth-first search from each unvisited node in increasing order. Starting from the lowest unvisited node makes the components come out ordered by their smallest member, and each component is sorted before it is appended.\n\nAll three methods validate node ids through the existing range check, so out-of-range ids still raise `IndexError`.",
